\ ff-test: lines mem=200000
\ Memory that Forth code asks for is checked: a size has to make sense,
\ and the engine stays within the host's limit (ff_platform::mem_limit),
\ here 200000 bytes.
\
\ `-1 array`, `-100 string` and a huge `allot` crashed the host: sizes
\ weren't validated, failed allocations weren't noticed, and memory given
\ to words was never handed back, not even by `forget`.

: p 32 emit . ;

\ A size a word can't use is an error (-24).
-1 array a
-100 string s
create x
0 allot
-5 allot
5 -1 dump
clear

\ More than the limit allows is refused (-8), and nothing is left
\ half-made.
x 1000000000000 allot
100000 array big
big
1000000 string huge
huge
clear

\ What fits still works.
10 array ok-arr
42 3 ok-arr ! 3 ok-arr @ p cr
20 string ok-str
"hello" ok-str s! ok-str type cr

\ `forget` gives the memory back: defining and forgetting a word three
\ thousand times stays within the limit.
: cycle 0 do ": tmp 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 + + + + + + + ; forget tmp" evaluate drop loop ;
3000 cycle
tmp
7 p cr

\ So does a definition that fails.
: failing 0 do ": broken 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 zork ;" evaluate drop loop ;
1000 failing
broken
8 p cr
